As required by Apache-2.0 §4(b), we state the changes. Modifications for DDC (this work):

  - managers/observation/terms/wbt.py
        added the deployable support-relative dynamic-CoM actor observation
        (`whole_body_com_rel_support_center`) and the privileged-critic xCoM observation
        (`whole_body_xcom_rel_support_center`), plus their CoM / capture-point helpers.

  - managers/reward/terms/wbt.py
        added the human-science balance reward library: capture-point / support-polygon
        Margin-of-Stability (`_support_polygon_margin`, `_convex_hull_halfspace_margin`),
        the xCoM computation (`_xcom_xy`) and support determination used by the balance rewards.

  - config_values/wbt/g1/{observation,reward,experiment}.py
        wired the above into the actor/critic observation groups, the reward weights
        (paper Table 6), and the FastSAC training hyperparameters (paper Table 6).

  - train_full.sh
        the multi-GPU FastSAC launch command for the DDC experiment.

These files are a small, readable SUBSET of Holosoma, provided so the DDC method is transparent and
reproducible in principle. They are NOT a redistribution of the full framework — install upstream
Holosoma (Apache-2.0) to run them; see TRAINING.md.
